course: dictionary
lesson: 3976
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Gag» is one of them. The dictionary gives it several meanings, so you need the context, which means the words around it, to find the right one.
explain: Read the sentence first. «The aunt asks to be gagged and bound and dumped down in a corner.» Here a gag is a piece of cloth put over someone's mouth, so they cannot shout. The words bound and dumped tell you this is not a joke.
explain: Now try a different sentence. «The comedian told a running gag about his cat.» A running gag is a joke that comes back again and again. The word comedian is your clue, because comedians tell jokes. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: "a running joke about his cat" still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: As a noun, a gag can be a joke or funny trick, or a piece of cloth put over someone's mouth to stop them shouting.
fact: As a verb, gag means to feel as if you are going to be sick, with your throat tightening. «The smell made me gag.»
fact: A gagging order is a rule that stops people talking publicly about something, such as in the news or in law.
fact: The word has the same spelling in every form, so context is the only way to tell which meaning is right.
exercise: «The aunt asks to be gagged, so it will look as if she was attacked.» In this sentence, what does gagged mean? | Felt sick at a bad smell | Was given a new hat | Told a funny joke | *Had a cloth put over her mouth to stop her shouting
exercise: «Rank!» she gags, then laughs. What does gags mean here? | Is telling a joke | Is tying a knot | *Feels as if she is going to be sick | Is shouting for help
exercise: The comedian told a «running gag» about his cat. What is a gag here? | A type of cat food | A cloth for the mouth | *A joke or funny trick | A law that stops people talking
test: A gagging order stops people from doing what? | *Talking publicly about something | Shouting at football matches | Telling jokes on the radio | Going to the seaside
test: «The smell from the bin made me gag.» What does gag mean? | Fall fast asleep | Shout very loudly | Laugh out loud | *Feel as if I am going to be sick
exam: In the story, the villain used a «gag» to stop the captive calling for help. What is the gag here? | *A cloth put over the captive's mouth | A map of the castle | A funny hat | A joke that made everyone laugh
